TOOL_START {"run_id": "r-4ab5d6f2de70-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0369-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0369-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m04", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0369-p0001", "phase_id": "phase1", "workday": 1, "simulation_time": "2025-05-05T09:00:00.008000+08:00", "step": 1, "workflow_id": "software_feature", "call_id": "tool-be5a43cf7dca44aa96e3c6f0eb1731fe", "provider_call_id": "call_2ccbfad485104491b2de40a9", "from_state": "issue_created", "tool_name": "design_document", "requested_tool_name": "design_document", "event_type": "tool_started", "status": "started", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 8, "event_id": "9477d108780b44969b5f9687941173b9", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:51:57.362986+00:00", "simulation_clock_kind": "task_start_plus_logical_order"}
TOOL_EVENT {"run_id": "r-4ab5d6f2de70-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0369-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0369-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m04", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0369-p0001", "phase_id": "phase1", "workday": 1, "simulation_time": "2025-05-05T09:00:00.009000+08:00", "step": 1, "workflow_id": "software_feature", "call_id": "tool-be5a43cf7dca44aa96e3c6f0eb1731fe", "provider_call_id": "call_2ccbfad485104491b2de40a9", "from_state": "issue_created", "tool_name": "design_document", "requested_tool_name": "design_document", "event_type": "tool_call", "to_state": "designed", "arguments": {"content": "Design document for compute(a, b) arithmetic mean feature.\n\n## Goal\nProvide a Python feature that computes the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs via compute(a, b) in src/main.py, with the core logic implemented in mean_values(a, b) in src/helper.py and reused through an import. A unittest in tests/test_compute.py verifies the documented behavior.\n\n## Requirements\n1. src/helper.py defines mean_values(a, b) returning (a + b) / 2.\n2. src/main.py defines compute(a, b) that imports mean_values from helper and returns its result.\n3. compute(2, 3) must return 2.5 (true division, not integer division).\n4. Zero, negative and fractional values must be supported, e.g. compute(0, -4) == -2.0, compute(-1.5, 2.5) == 0.5.\n5. Inputs must be finite numbers (int or float, excluding bool); non-numeric or non-finite inputs (NaN, inf) raise ValueError.\n6. tests/test_compute.py contains a unittest.TestCase asserting compute(2, 3) == 2.5 plus additional coverage for zero, negative, fractional and error cases.\n\n## Architecture\n- helper.py is the pure computation module: mean_values(a, b) performs validation (finite numeric check) and returns the arithmetic mean using true division.\n- main.py is the public entry point: it imports mean_values from helper and delegates; compute(a, b) is a thin wrapper so the public API stays stable.\n- tests/test_compute.py uses the standard library unittest module and imports compute from src.main.\n\n## Validation plan\n- Run tests/test_compute.py with unittest.\n- Run the public behavioral check: /opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py.\n- Build with /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src.\n\n## Edge cases\n- Integer inputs must produce a float mean (2, 3 -> 2.5) via true division.\n- Negative and zero inputs are ordinary finite numbers and are accepted.\n- bool is a subclass of int but is rejected as a non-numeric-meaningful input to avoid ambiguity.\n- NaN and infinity raise ValueError because the mean would not be a finite number.\n", "input_artifact_id": "219a5f816118"}, "result": {"tool_name": "design_document", "message": "design document created", "output_artifact_ids": ["4445cec17455"], "output_paths": ["artifacts/4445cec17455.md"], "evidence_level": "simulation_only", "business_status": "not_measured", "payload": "Design document for compute(a, b) arithmetic mean feature.\n\n## Goal\nProvide a Python feature that computes the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs via compute(a, b) in src/main.py, with the core logic implemented in mean_values(a, b) in src/helper.py and reused through an import. A unittest in tests/test_compute.py verifies the documented behavior.\n\n## Requirements\n1. src/helper.py defines mean_values(a, b) returning (a + b) / 2.\n2. src/main.py defines compute(a, b) that imports mean_values from helper and returns its result.\n3. compute(2, 3) must return 2.5 (true division, not integer division).\n4. Zero, negative and fractional values must be supported, e.g. compute(0, -4) == -2.0, compute(-1.5, 2.5) == 0.5.\n5. Inputs must be finite numbers (int or float, excluding bool); non-numeric or non-finite inputs (NaN, inf) raise ValueError.\n6. tests/test_compute.py contains a unittest.TestCase asserting compute(2, 3) == 2.5 plus additional coverage for zero, negative, fractional and error cases.\n\n## Architecture\n- helper.py is the pure computation module: mean_values(a, b) performs validation (finite numeric check) and returns the arithmetic mean using true division.\n- main.py is the public entry point: it imports mean_values from helper and delegates; compute(a, b) is a thin wrapper so the public API stays stable.\n- tests/test_compute.py uses the standard library unittest module and imports compute from src.main.\n\n## Validation plan\n- Run tests/test_compute.py with unittest.\n- Run the public behavioral check: /opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py.\n- Build with /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src.\n\n## Edge cases\n- Integer inputs must produce a float mean (2, 3 -> 2.5) via true division.\n- Negative and zero inputs are ordinary finite numbers and are accepted.\n- bool is a subclass of int but is rejected as a non-numeric-meaningful input to avoid ambiguity.\n- NaN and infinity raise ValueError because the mean would not be a finite number.\n", "output_paths_kind": "read_only_capture_evidence", "business_path": null, "workspace": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0369/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0369-t0001", "execution_environment": {"cwd": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0369/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0369-t0001", "python_executable": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python", "default_build_command": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src", "build_kind": "python_bytecode_compilation", "optional_modules": {"pytest": true, "build": false, "pip": true, "setuptools": true}}}, "status": "success", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 9, "event_id": "08687fda3c4e4bb088c82e83b85798a5", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:51:57.368102+00:00", "simulation_clock_kind": "task_start_plus_logical_order"}
