FINAL_EVENT {"run_id": "r-4ab5d6f2de70-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0369-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0369-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m04", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0369-p0001", "phase_id": "phase1", "workday": 1, "simulation_time": "2025-05-05T09:00:00.040000+08:00", "event_type": "final_answer", "workflow_id": "software_feature", "state": "completed", "answer": "Feature complete and approved. Summary:\n\n- **src/helper.py** — `mean_values(a, b)` computes the arithmetic mean with true division (`(a + b) / 2`), validating that inputs are finite real numbers (rejects bool, non-numeric, NaN, ±inf with `ValueError`).\n- **src/main.py** — `compute(a, b)` imports and delegates to `helper.mean_values`; `compute(2, 3)` returns `2.5`, with zero, negative and fractional values supported.\n- **tests/test_compute.py** — unittest suite covering the required `compute(2, 3) == 2.5` check plus true division, zero/negative/fractional cases, symmetry, and error handling.\n\nValidation: `checks/public_check.py` passed (returncode 0), and the build `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src` succeeded. The pull request was opened and the simulated review/approval phase finished with approval granted.", "status": "completed", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 40, "event_id": "d9c99925d59a4e28816201277805d251", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:53:15.811455+00:00", "simulation_clock_kind": "task_start_plus_logical_order"}
